for other reservations on the same date/court with pendente or confirmada status (not avulsa in-process) that overlap the cancelled hours, treating the slot as replaced only if all cancelled hours are fully covered by paid replacement bookings rather than trying to handle partial coverage.\\n\\nFor the lead-time calculation, I need a function comparing the notice date to the reservation date in calendar days, where the admin can either default to today's date or manually input an earlier warning date if the group communicated via WhatsApp beforehand.\\n\\nI'm also thinking cancellation should only apply to future occurrences, not past ones, and I want to add a restore function for reverting a cancellation when no conflicting reservation has taken the slot yet — checking for conflicts through a pure validation function. For contract creation, I need to generate the occurrence dates and validate each against existing active reservations on the same court and overlapping hours, deciding whether to block the whole creation or only skip conflicting dates.\\n\\nBlocking seems safer since it forces the admin to resolve existing single bookings first, and since occurrences become materialized reservations, conflicts with other contracts get caught too — client-side validation is enough given the existing app has the same limitation. For calculating dates, I need a helper that finds the first occurrence on or after the start date matching the chosen weekday, then generates subsequent occurrences by adding months up to the contract length.\\n\\nFor persistence, I'll build Supabase-backed services for contracts (fetch, insert, update, remove) plus a bulk insert for reservations, using deterministic IDs combining contract ID and date so inserts stay idempotent and unique.\\n\\nI'm thinking through where contract data gets loaded — probably a `useContratosService` hook mirroring the reservas pattern, with optimistic local updates plus async remote sync and a localStorage fallback when Supabase isn't configured. For the portal banners, I need to cross-reference reservas with tipoReserva \\\"escolinha\\\" and non-cancelled status back to their contract to display per-date, per-quadra occupancy info.\\n\\nI also need an \\\"encerrar contrato\\\" flow that cancels all future occurrences and sets ativo to false, plus corresponding row/object mapping updates for the new contrato_id, tipo_reserva, and aviso_cancelamento_em fields, with graceful fallback if those columns don't exist yet in the database.\\n\\nIf the Supabase migration hasn't been run, contract creation could succeed locally but fail remotely, so I should flag that users need to apply the schema.sql update. For the UI, I'm planning a generic admin page component parametrized by contract type, with thin wrapper components for each specific use case.\\n\\nNow I'm mapping out the actual differences between escolinha and grupo flows: escolinha needs sport, description, and public contact fields, while grupo needs group name, responsible person, and billing value info, each with their own occurrence detail views. Grupos get a cancellation-with-notice flow and billing status tracking, while escolinhas skip cancellation entirely and only support ending the contract outright, so I'm sketching out the file structure for these recurring admin components accordingly.\\n\\nTo avoid component API mismatches, I'll opt for plain HTML inputs with tailwind and an inline collapsible panel instead of a modal, toggled by a \\\"Novo\\\" button, and use sonner for toasts. I'll create `useContratosService` hook and `useContratosStore`, with the hook's `criarContrato` mutation returning success/error/conflict info and coordinating with the reservas store.\\n\\nNow I'm building the lib functions for validating contract data, generating occurrences, detecting conflicts, and assembling reservation occurrences, starting with date utility functions for parsing, formatting, adding days/months, and computing weekday and date differences.\\n\\nI need to handle month-overflow edge cases when adding months (clamping to the last day of the target month), and I'm working out the logic for generating recurring dates by stepping weekly from a start date until a calculated end date, plus expanding time slots into hourly blocks while validating against allowed schedule windows.\\n\\nNow I'm sketching validation rules for a contract form — required name, phone digit length, valid court, time ordering, slot availability, month range, and ensuring the start date isn't in the past (using an injectable \\\"today\\\" for testability). I'm also considering whether the weekday should be derived from the chosen start date, and whether a single contract should support multiple weekdays.\\n\\nI'm deciding to support an array of weekdays since escolinhas often meet twice a week, with occurrence generation looping through dates and filtering by matching weekdays, all sharing the same time slot, stored as an integer array column. Then I'm designing a function to build occurrence dates from a contract and another to convert each occurrence into a reservation object with a composite ID and client fields pulled from the contract.\\n\\nFor values, I'm setting escolinha reservations as fully confirmed with zero amounts, while group reservations calculate the total from the hourly rate with no sinal paid, leaving everything pending — checking that this flows correctly into dashboards showing today's reservations, since these would be real entries. I'm also considering cancellation rules next.\\n\\nNow I'm defining the cancellation module: a constant for minimum notice days, a classification function distinguishing penalty-free versus late notice based on how far in advance the cancellation was registered, and a function checking whether a cancellation can even be logged for a given reservation on a given day. I'm also adding logic to determine charge status — whether a cancelled slot is penalty-free, awaiting makeup, exempt due to makeup, or actually owed — by checking if the cancelled occurrence was rescheduled among all reservations, and I'm working through what happens when a cancellation has no recorded notice timestamp.\\n\\nI'm treating contract terminations (cancelled with no notice date) as automatically penalty-free, and storing the notice date as a plain DATE column rather than a timestamp for simplicity. For classification, a gap of 7+ days between notice and the slot date is penalty-free, otherwise it's late; for late cancellations, I check if a makeup slot was booked (exempt), if the date has already passed without one (charge owed), or if it's still pending (awaiting makeup). I'm also considering the edge case where notice comes after the reservation date itself.\\n\\nI need to validate that notice dates can't be set in the future or after the actual occurrence date. I'm also writing logic to determine if a cancelled reservation was fully covered by replacement bookings on the same date/court/hours, and defining a conflict-detection function that checks active reservations plus in-progress locks against requested time slots.\\n\\nFor reactivating an occurrence, I need to check for conflicts with other active overlapping reservations. I'm also sketching out a function that groups escolinha reservations by date and court to generate notices with contract details like name, sport, and time range.\\n\\nThe contract lookup can fall back to reserva fields when the contract isn't loaded, so banners work even without the contracts table loaded. I'm now designing the portal components: a banner showing the escolinha schedule info and a modal, with text describing the class name, sport, and time window.\\n\\nFor the modal, I'll include days of week from the contract, a description, and a WhatsApp link using the normalized phone number without the plus sign, plus a \\\"matricule-se\\\" button. I should check the existing dialog component's API first so I build